  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔧 Step 5: Generate Technical Indicators\n",
    "\n",
    "### Academic Justification:\n",
    "- **Momentum** (Jegadeesh & Titman, 1993): Past returns predict future returns\n",
    "- **Volatility** (Ang et al., 2006): Idiosyncratic volatility affects returns\n",
    "- **Technical Analysis** (Brock et al., 1992): Simple indicators have predictive power"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Generating technical indicators for each stock...\")\n",
    "print(\"This will take several minutes...\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare volume data\n",
    "volume_pivot = prices_df.pivot_table(\n",
    "    index='datadate',\n",
    "    columns='gvkey',\n",
    "    values='cshtrd'\n",
    ").sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize storage\n",
    "all_technical_features = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for gvkey in tqdm(price_pivot.columns, desc=\"Computing technicals\"):\n",
    "    prices = price_pivot[gvkey].dropna()\n",
    "    volumes = volume_pivot[gvkey].dropna() if gvkey in volume_pivot.columns else pd.Series()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Technical indicators\n",
    "    rsi = TechnicalIndicators.calculate_rsi(prices, period=config.RSI_PERIOD)\n",
    "    macd, macd_signal = TechnicalIndicators.calculate_macd(\n",
    "        prices,\n",
    "        fast=config.MACD_FAST,\n",
    "        slow=config.MACD_SLOW,\n",
    "        signal=config.MACD_SIGNAL\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    bb_upper, bb_middle, bb_lower = TechnicalIndicators.calculate_bollinger_bands(\n",
    "        prices,\n",
    "        period=config.BOLLINGER_PERIOD,\n",
    "        num_std=config.BOLLINGER_STD\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    returns_multi = TechnicalIndicators.calculate_returns(prices, config.RETURNS_WINDOW)\n",
    "    volatility = TechnicalIndicators.calculate_volatility(\n",
    "        prices.pct_change(),\n",
    "        window=config.VOLATILITY_WINDOW\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Combine into DataFrame\n",
    "    tech_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "        'gvkey': gvkey,\n",
    "        'date': prices.index,\n",
    "        'rsi': rsi,\n",
    "        'macd': macd,\n",
    "        'macd_signal': macd_signal,\n",
    "        'bb_upper': bb_upper,\n",
    "        'bb_middle': bb_middle,\n",
    "        'bb_lower': bb_lower,\n",
    "        'volatility': volatility\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add multi-window returns\n",
    "    for col in returns_multi.columns:\n",
    "        tech_df[col] = returns_multi[col].values\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add volume MA if available\n",
    "    if len(volumes) > 0:\n",
    "        tech_df['volume_ma'] = volumes.rolling(window=config.VOLUME_MA_PERIOD).mean().values\n",
    "    \n",
    "    all_technical_features.append(tech_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine all stocks\n",
    "technical_features = pd.concat(all_technical_features, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Generated technical features: {technical_features.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Features per stock: {len([c for c in technical_features.columns if c not in ['gvkey', 'date']])}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "technical_features.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🎯 Step 6: Apply PCA (Dimensionality Reduction)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Academic Justification (Connor & Korajczyk, 1988):\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why PCA?**\n",
    "1. **Curse of Dimensionality**: 20+ features lead to overfitting\n",
    "2. **Multicollinearity**: Many technical indicators are correlated\n",
    "3. **Factor Models**: PCA extracts latent factors (like Fama-French)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Critical**: We fit PCA **only on training data** to prevent look-ahead bias!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create train/val/test masks\n",
    "print(\"Creating train/validation/test splits...\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "technical_features['date'] = pd.to_datetime(technical_features['date'])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_mask = (technical_features['date'] >= config.TRAIN_START) & \\\n",
    "             (technical_features['date'] <= config.TRAIN_END)\n",
    "val_mask = (technical_features['date'] >= config.VALIDATION_START) & \\\n",
    "           (technical_features['date'] <= config.VALIDATION_END)\n",
    "test_mask = (technical_features['date'] >= config.TEST_START) & \\\n",
    "            (technical_features['date'] <= config.TEST_END)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training set:   {train_mask.sum():,} samples ({config.TRAIN_START} to {config.TRAIN_END})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation set: {val_mask.sum():,} samples ({config.VALIDATION_START} to {config.VALIDATION_END})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test set:       {test_mask.sum():,} samples ({config.TEST_START} to {config.TEST_END})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n⚠️  CRITICAL: PCA will be fit ONLY on training data to prevent look-ahead bias!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize feature engineer\n",
    "feat_engineer = FeatureEngineer(\n",
    "    beta_window=config.BETA_WINDOW,\n",
    "    pca_variance_threshold=config.PCA_VARIANCE_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "    fit_on_train_only=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Applying PCA to technical features...\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target variance explained: {config.PCA_VARIANCE_THRESHOLD * 100}%\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply PCA\n",
    "pca_features, pca_model = feat_engineer.apply_pca(\n",
    "    technical_features=technical_features,\n",
    "    train_mask=train_mask\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "n_components = pca_model.n_components_\n",
    "explained_var = pca_model.explained_variance_ratio_\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ PCA reduced {len(technical_features.columns)-2} features to {n_components} components\")\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Total variance explained: {explained_var.sum():.2%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot explained variance\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Individual variance\n",
    "axes[0].bar(range(1, n_components+1), explained_var)\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Principal Component')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Variance Explained')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Variance Explained by Each Component')\n",
    "axes[0].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cumulative variance\n",
    "cumulative_var = np.cumsum(explained_var)\n",
    "axes[1].plot(range(1, n_components+1), cumulative_var, marker='o')\n",
    "axes[1].axhline(config.PCA_VARIANCE_THRESHOLD, color='red', linestyle='--', \n",
    "                label=f'Threshold: {config.PCA_VARIANCE_THRESHOLD:.0%}')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Number of Components')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Cumulative Variance Explained')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Cumulative Variance Explained')\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "axes[1].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
