    "## 🎯 Step 8: Create Binary Target Variable\n",
    "\n",
    "**Target:**\n",
    "$$y_t = \\begin{cases} \n",
    "1 & \\text{if } r_{\\text{residual},t} > 0 \\\\\n",
    "0 & \\text{otherwise}\n",
    "\\end{cases}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why binary classification?**\n",
    "- Predicting exact returns is very difficult (low R²)\n",
    "- Direction (up/down) is more robust\n",
    "- Standard in ML finance literature (Gu et al., 2020)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
